cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Lossless BF16 weight compression: entropy code vs. memory layout, a measured refutation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ferrerons Manich"
    given-names: "Arnau"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-7245-7221"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ArnauFerma/bf16-exponent-compression"
date-released: 2026-09-13
abstract: >-
  Lossless compression of BF16 model weights by entropy-coding the exponent
  field, in the same family as DFloat11. Tests the hypothesis that a small
  "ladder" prefix code beats canonical Huffman on GPU decode speed; measures
  that it does not, and that the memory access pattern and the block index
  dominate decoder performance instead. Includes CUDA kernels, measurement
  harnesses and a full methodology.
keywords:
  - lossless compression
  - bfloat16
  - entropy coding
  - Huffman
  - CUDA
  - LLM weights
  - negative result
license: MIT
